# Git Workflow

## The pipeline

`main` is the production branch. **Pushing to `main` deploys.** Cloudflare Pages
(project `dr-david-ogbueli`) is connected to the GitHub repo and auto-builds every
push. There is no separate release step.

- Do **not** use local `wrangler pages deploy out` as the deploy path — sustained
  local uploads to Cloudflare's asset endpoint time out from this network. Git-connected
  deploy is the reliable path.
- Check deploys: `npx wrangler pages deployment list --project-name dr-david-ogbueli`.

## Account

Three GitHub accounts may be logged in; **only `dominioncitychurchajah` has push
access.** If a push 403s, switch:

```bash
gh auth switch --hostname github.com --user dominioncitychurchajah
```

## Commit hygiene

- **Stage only the files you intended to change.** The repo root has untracked spec
  files (`*-build-spec-*.md`, `start-here-ai.html`, etc.) — never blanket `git add .`.
- Never commit secrets or personal access tokens.
- End commit messages with:
  `Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>`
- Don't run destructive commands (`git reset --hard`, force-push) unless explicitly asked.
- Don't revert unrelated work.

## Confirm before deploying

Pushing publishes to a live site. Confirm intent with the user before pushing unless
they've clearly authorized it for the change at hand.
